    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` which asserts `membershipLevel == 3`.\n\nHere's what I changed to satisfy the spec:\n\n**Numeric level, computed on creation**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a persisted `membershipLevel` (`membership_level` column) with getter/setter.\n- New `AssignMembershipLevel.java` function: starts at 1, `+1` if email present, `+1` if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 left reserved for tenure).\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` after `assignNamesakeCount` (so the namesake snapshot and normalized email are already set) and before `assignMembershipNumber`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n- Added the `membership_level` column to all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Response: `membershipTier` \u2192 `membershipLevel`**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string enum with a `membershipLevel` integer (min 1, max 3), regenerating `OwnerDto` accordingly.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 dropped the `membershipTier` expression mapping and the `membershipTier(...)` derivation method; `membershipLevel` now maps straight through by name from the stored field.\n\n**Audit records the level**\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the create audit line now includes `membershipLevel={}`.\n\nI also cleaned up a now-stale doc comment in `AssignHouseholdSize.java` that referenced the removed GOLD tier. Note the previous tier was derived at read time from household size; the new level is assigned once at creation and stored, which is what the audit-line requirement implies.",
